<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Ansett to seek more Japan flights.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Ansett to seek more Japan flights.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ansett Airline said it would seek permission to expand its Australia-Japan services to seven a week from five following the Australia-Japan agreement to increase airline capacity announced earlier by Canberra.</p>
<p>The agreement allowed extra flights from Osaka, a strong growth market for Australian inbound tourism, Ansett said.</p>
<p>If its application succeeded, Ansett would operate daily Boeing 747 Osaka-Brisbane-Sydney-Osaka flights, it said.</p>
<p>Ansett is owned 50/50 by The News Corp Ltd and Air New Zealand Ltd.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
